# Two keys and you are running:
#
#   export ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
#   export TAVILY_API_KEY=tvly-...
#   uv run python -m superforecaster serve
#
# This file exists for when you want them to persist, or when you are deploying.
# Real environment variables win over anything set here.

# ---------- the two keys ----------

# The model. console.anthropic.com
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Web search, used by every research agent. Free tier at tavily.com.
# Without it the agents fall back to Wikipedia alone — the run still completes, but the
# reference classes it finds are noticeably thinner, and the header says so.
TAVILY_API_KEY=

# Route the model through the Logfire Gateway instead of calling Anthropic directly.
# logfire.pydantic.dev -> org -> Gateway. Legacy paig_... keys no longer work.
# PYDANTIC_AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY=

# ---------- only when you deploy this ----------

# Required to start a forecast from anywhere other than localhost. Unset, the API accepts
# unauthenticated admin requests from 127.0.0.1 and refuses them from everywhere else —
# which is what makes the two-key local setup work. Set it before exposing the port.
# ADMIN_API_KEY=

# ---------- optional ----------

# Wikipedia is read anonymously and works without this. A Wikimedia access token only
# raises the rate limit. Settable from the Keys panel in the app, for this process only.
# WIKIPEDIA_API_KEY=

# AGENT_MODEL=anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6      # override the model for every agent
# LOGFIRE_TOKEN=                               # pylf_v1_... write token for cloud traces
# DATABASE_PATH=./superforecaster.db           # Docker uses /app/data/superforecaster.db

# Per-agent budgets. Four ceilings each — cost in dollars, tokens, tool calls, and
# iterations (model requests) — in that order, comma-separated. One variable per agent,
# named BUDGET_<AGENT>. Defaults live in `config.BUDGETS`; set one only to override it.
# BUDGET_BASE_RATE_CELL=0.40,200000,8,11       # one column at the base-rate stage
# BUDGET_INSIDE_VIEW=0.40,200000,8,11          # one column at the adjust stage
# BUDGET_CRITIC=0.10,60000,3,6                 # the resolvability check
# BUDGET_RESOLUTION=0.10,60000,4,7
# BUDGET_UPDATE=0.10,60000,4,7
# BUDGET_POSTMORTEM=0.10,60000,4,7
# BUDGET_DECOMPOSE=0.15,80000,0,4              # tool calls are 0: no search tools
# BUDGET_LENSES=0.15,80000,0,4
# BUDGET_REFLECT=0.20,100000,0,4
# BUDGET_SYNTHESIZE=0.25,120000,0,4
# BUDGET_DRAFT=0.10,40000,0,4

# Deadlines. A usage limit bounds how many times an agent may act; these bound how long
# it may take. Every stall this system has produced was a request that never came back,
# which reaches no limit and raises nothing — so without these a step never ends and the
# browser sits on a loading state forever. Set either to 0 to disable. There is no
# whole-run timeout: a gated run is supposed to sit idle at a gate indefinitely; only
# the work between two clicks is bounded.
# AGENT_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=180                    # one agent run
# STAGE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=600                    # one gated step (a handful of agent runs)

# Output-token ceiling per model response. The provider default (4096) is too small for
# the synthesize agent's structured output — a truncated response raises
# IncompleteToolCall and a retry hits the same wall.
# AGENT_MAX_TOKENS=16384

# The synthesis agent may move the final probability at most this far from the number
# the arithmetic implies (the ±5-point rule).
# CHECK_DERIVATION_SLACK=0.05

# REFRESH_CRON_SCHEDULE=0 6 * * *
# MIN_PROBABILITY_DELTA=0.03
# SEARCH_LOOKBACK_HOURS=48
